id=a52sxq_home_depth_clock
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: home-screen depth clock (prototype, off by default)
author=kusti420
description=Draws a large clock on the home wallpaper between the background and the cut-out subject when the home wallpaper is a Samsung layered wallpaper (Gallery -> wallpaper editor). SpriteWallpaper's engine factory (c3.a.a) normally gives the home-only instance (which & 3 == 1) a FlattenLayeredPresenter (h3.d) that bakes all layers into one bitmap; with persist.sys.k4.home_depth_clock=1 HomeDepthClock.presenter() returns HomeClockPresenter instead, which loads the layers through the stock LayeredPresenter (h3.f, WallpaperManager asset file descriptors), flattens them into two screen-sized bitmaps split at the subject node and puts a ClockNode between them. LayeredEngine (f3.a) onVisibilityChanged/onDestroy start/stop an ACTION_TIME_TICK receiver while the home wallpaper is visible; it redraws only when the shown minute is stale (no per-frame drawing, no wakeups). Unset/0 = stock code path (the hooks only return early). Tunables (read at engine start): persist.sys.k4.home_depth_clock_y = digit centre in % of screen height, persist.sys.k4.home_depth_clock_color = #RRGGBB. Apply a change by restarting com.samsung.android.wallpaper.live (kill the process, never force-stop: that resets the wallpaper). Signed with aosp_platform like every rebuilt APK; the signature patch maps that to the platform signature, and the app has no sharedUserId.
